    "note": "Today against a month ago. The front end eased on Friday — the two-year fell to 4.81% and is lower on the week — while the twenty- and thirty-year rose, so the curve steepened as it sold off; every maturity from three years out still yields close to 5% or more. Reported closes on Friday were about 4.86% on the two-year, 5.18% on the ten and 5.50% on the thirty; the source table prints 4.81%, 5.17% and 5.49%, which is what the curve above draws. No coupon supply this week; the ten-year and thirty-year auctions land on 7 and 8 October.",
